I have a suggestion for another preference (as if there arent enough :); ; Im not sure when exactly the following changed:; ; The old and the new formatter (at least up to some point 2/3 months ago) would; not strip the last 
 of a file.; ; So if one had:; ; 1: class Test {
; 2: }
; 3:
EOF; ; The formatter would leave it as is.; ; Right now the above gets formatted to:; ; 1: class Test {
; 2: }
EOF; ; Im not totally sure; but I remember reading about some Linux tools and/or CMS; having problems if a text file does not have a final line only containing 
.; ; Heres a related link from Checkstyle:; http://checkstyle.sourceforge.net/config_misc.html#NewlineAtEndOfFile

